</head>
<body>
  <header class="guide-header">
    <a class="guide-brand" href="/" aria-label="QuizMaster Pro home">QuizMaster <span>Pro</span></a>
    <nav aria-label="Main navigation">
      <a href="/">Home</a>
      <a class="guide-nav-cta" href="/login">Sign in or create an account</a>
    </nav>
  </header>

  <main class="guide-main">
    <section class="guide-hero" aria-labelledby="guideTitle">
      <p class="guide-eyebrow">QUIZMASTER PRO GUIDE</p>
      <h1 id="guideTitle">How to create and take online exams</h1>
      <p>QuizMaster Pro helps teachers prepare questions, assign scheduled exams and review results. Students sign in to take their assigned exams and see results when they are released.</p>
      <a class="guide-primary-link" href="/login">Get started</a>
    </section>

    <nav class="guide-contents" aria-label="On this page">
      <strong>On this page</strong>
      <a href="#teachers">For teachers</a>
      <a href="#students">For students</a>
      <a href="#results">Results and written answers</a>
      <a href="#questions">Question formats</a>
    </nav>

    <section class="guide-section" id="teachers" aria-labelledby="teachersTitle">
      <p class="guide-eyebrow">TEACHER WORKFLOW</p>
      <h2 id="teachersTitle">Create and assign an exam</h2>
      <ol class="guide-steps">
        <li><h3>Create a teacher account</h3><p>Open <a href="/login">Sign in or create an account</a>, choose the Teacher role when registering, then sign in to open the teacher workspace.</p></li>
        <li><h3>Build a question bank</h3><p>Create questions one at a time or use <strong>Paste many questions</strong> to import up to 100 multiple-choice questions in a batch. Set the subject and class, review the parsed questions and answer keys, then save them.</p></li>
        <li><h3>Set up the exam</h3><p>Choose questions from your question bank, add the exam title and subject, and set the start time, end time, attempt duration and marks. Negative marking and retakes can be configured where needed.</p></li>
        <li><h3>Assign students and choose result visibility</h3><p>Select the registered students who should take the exam. Choose whether results appear immediately, after the exam window closes, or only after you release them.</p></li>
        <li><h3>Review progress and submissions</h3><p>Use the teacher results area to review attempts and score summaries. Written-answer submissions need teacher review and grading before the result can be finalized.</p></li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="guide-section guide-section-tint" id="students" aria-labelledby="studentsTitle">
      <p class="guide-eyebrow">STUDENT WORKFLOW</p>
      <h2 id="studentsTitle">Take an assigned exam</h2>
      <ol class="guide-steps">
        <li><h3>Create a student account</h3><p>Register from the <a href="/login">account page</a> and choose Student. Enter your class or grade if requested, then sign in.</p></li>
        <li><h3>Open an active exam</h3><p>Your teacher must assign an exam to your account. Open Active Exams and check the exam instructions, scheduled window, duration and marks before starting.</p></li>
        <li><h3>Answer and submit</h3><p>Answer the multiple-choice questions or attach a file for a written-answer question when enabled. Submit before the timer expires and confirm the submission if prompted.</p></li>
        <li><h3>Check your result</h3><p>Open Results when the teacher's result-visibility setting allows it. A written-answer result may remain pending until the teacher grades the submission.</p></li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="guide-section" id="results" aria-labelledby="resultsTitle">
      <p class="guide-eyebrow">SCORING AND REVIEW</p>
      <h2 id="resultsTitle">How results are handled</h2>
      <p>Multiple-choice answers are scored automatically using the answer key saved with each question. Exam marks, negative marking and result release timing follow the settings chosen by the teacher. Written answers are reviewed by the teacher, who enters a mark and feedback before releasing the result.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="guide-section guide-section-tint" id="questions" aria-labelledby="questionsTitle">
      <p class="guide-eyebrow">QUESTION CREATION</p>
      <h2 id="questionsTitle">Supported question formats</h2>
      <ul class="guide-feature-list">
        <li><strong>Multiple choice:</strong> add answer choices and mark the correct answer. In a batch paste, use four choices per question and a matching answer line.</li>
        <li><strong>Written answer:</strong> ask students to submit a written response; the teacher grades it after submission.</li>
        <li><strong>Math questions:</strong> the question creator supports mathematical notation and preview tools.</li>
        <li><strong>Batch MCQ labels:</strong> use A-D, a-d, I-IV, i-iv, or Bengali ক-ঘ consistently within each question.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="guide-faq" aria-labelledby="faqTitle">
      <p class="guide-eyebrow">COMMON QUESTIONS</p>
      <h2 id="faqTitle">Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <details><summary>Why can a student not see an exam?</summary><p>The teacher needs to assign the exam to that student's registered account. The exam must also be within its scheduled start and end times.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Why is a result still pending?</summary><p>The teacher may have chosen to release results later, or a written answer may still need manual grading.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Can teachers paste many MCQs at once?</summary><p>Yes. The batch creator accepts up to 100 MCQs at a time. Review the parsed questions and correct answers before saving.</p></details>
    </section>

    <section class="guide-end">
      <h2>Ready to prepare an exam?</h2>
      <p>Sign in or create an account to start using QuizMaster Pro.</p>
      <a class="guide-primary-link" href="/login">Open QuizMaster Pro</a>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer class="guide-footer"><a href="/">QuizMaster Pro</a><a href="/about">About the creator</a><span>Online exams and quizzes for teachers and students</span></footer>
</body>
</html>
